// A list of lists of records of an un-annotated function, delivered at every position, then a
// whole list literal of records of another function pushed onto it and both called at two types
// (D15357). The pushed literal's inner records are built at the holder's element row.
//
// Format: scripts/capability-probes/README.md, "Template format".
// @@PRELUDE@@
function __idA(a) { return a + 1 }
function __idB(a) { return a * 10 }
// @@VALUE@@
[[{ f: __idA }]]
// @@TYPE@@
{ f: (a: f64) => f64 }[][]
// @@PROOF@@
v.push([{ f: __idB }])
print("\{v[1][0].f(2)},\{v[0][0].f(2.5)},\{v.length}")
// @@WANT@@
20,3.5,2
// @@SKIP@@
is_in_if: the value is a list, not a union — there is no arm to test it against
is_in_while: same
is_in_and: same
is_in_not: same
else_if: same
early_return_guard: same
